From 0f334c797705530bf990c2fd17783ce26bcea59f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PapyElGringo <adrien@pesler.be>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 12:57:04 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] [embedder] Damage only what changed in an external texture's
 new frame

With texture layers left undamaged when their texture has no new frame,
a texture that does present one still damages its whole area, however
little of it changed: a blinking text cursor in a window repaints the
whole window, along with whatever filters it (a blur over it re-runs
over the whole blurred area).

FlutterEngineMarkExternalTextureFrameAvailableWithInfo takes the size of
the new frame and its damage (a FlutterDamage, in pixels of the frame),
the texture counterpart of the existing damage callbacks:
FlutterEngineMarkExternalTextureFrameAvailable marks a frame damaged as a
whole. The embedder records each frame's damage on the platform thread;
the texture takes it on the raster thread with the matching
MarkNewFrameAvailable, and keeps the damage of its last frames.

A texture reports the damage since a given frame (Texture::GetDamageSince),
unknown when that frame is too old, when one of the frames since had no
damage, or when the frame size changed. TextureLayer maps it onto its
bounds, with a margin for the sampling filter (the whole layer when the
texture is mipmapped), and adds it with DiffContext::AddLayerDamage, which
applies the same transform, filter bounds adjustments and culling as layer
bounds without marking the subtree dirty.
